gXy(){return"The motor circuit breaker (MPCB) protects the motor: rotary 0/I handle, thermal Ir dial, magneto-thermal trip. Terminals 1/L1\xb73/L2\xb75/L3 upstream and 2/T1\xb74/T2\xb76/T3 toward the motor."},
gXH(){return"The RE17 timer relay delays or pulses a contact according to the set time (functions A to Di).\n\nTerminals\n- A1 and A2: supply\n- 15, 16 and 18: changeover contact (15 common, 16 NC, 18 NO)\n- Y1: control input (At, C, Ac, B) \u2014 not a second coil.\n\nSettings\n- Time range and multiplier (1 to 10)\n- Function on the bottom dial\n\nFunctions\n- A: on-delay (TON) from A1\u2013A2\n- At: like A, with pause/summation: Y1 closed = pause (elapsed time is kept)\n- C: Y1 ON \u2192 18 immediately; Y1 OFF \u2192 delay then 18 opens (A1\u2013A2 stay powered)\n- Ac: delay on Y1 closing AND on Y1 opening\n- B: one-shot pulse commanded by Y1\n- D and Di: flasher from A1\u2013A2"},
